cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      # OML K-means: tree groups for the existing supervised team


      Pilot question: How do Quercus robur (oak) trees group by recorded
      TREE_AGE

      (numeric) and TRUNK_DIAMETER (categorical class), and where are those

      trees? The source is BOMEN_TREES. SVM flags and density values are not

      model inputs. A cluster is a description of records, not a health claim.


      The tool creates its own storage, trains when the source or cluster count

      changes, saves all scored tree points, and returns a RUN_ID. The existing

      APEX GET_RESPONSE can read their GeoJSON from AGENT_MAP_RESULTS. All map

      points are saved; a large response may take time in Ask Oracle.


      Prerequisite: BOMEN_TREES exists. Run this notebook after the density,

      SVM, and discovery worker definitions. The final cell replaces only the

      existing TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM and its supervisor, adding discovery and

      K-means workers. Run it when no team request is active. Tests live only

      in 2-bomen_OML_discovery_Kmeans_tests.sqlnb.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 1. Automatic storage setup

      Creates missing K-means tables and views, plus the shared map table if
      needed. Saved runs and rows are never dropped here.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "1- “Do you see any candidate issues in my tree datasets?”\r

      \r

      2- “Group Quercus robur trees into three clusters by age and
      trunk-diameter class.”\r

      \r

      3- “Show those tree clusters on the map.”"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE prepare_tree_kmeans_storage AS
          v_count NUMBER;
      BEGIN
          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN_TREES';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20300, 'BOMEN_TREES is missing.');
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID VARCHAR2(32) NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_RECORD_ID NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SPECIES_NAME VARCHAR2(254 CHAR),
                      TREE_AGE NUMBER,
                      TRUNK_DIAMETER VARCHAR2(50 CHAR),
                      CLUSTER_ID NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      CLUSTER_PROBABILITY NUMBER,
                      WGS84_LONGITUDE NUMBER,
                      WGS84_LATITUDE NUMBER,
                      GEOMETRY MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY,
                      CREATED_AT TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP,
                      CONSTRAINT TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS_PK
                          PRIMARY KEY (RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'TREE_KMEANS_RUNS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_KMEANS_RUNS (
                      RUN_ID VARCHAR2(32) PRIMARY KEY,
                      SPECIES_NAME VARCHAR2(254 CHAR) NOT NULL,
                      REQUESTED_CLUSTERS NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_ROW_COUNT NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_MAX_SCN NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SCORED_COUNT NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      CREATED_AT TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS (
                      SETTING_NAME VARCHAR2(30),
                      SETTING_VALUE VARCHAR2(4000)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'AGENT_MAP_RESULTS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE AGENT_MAP_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID VARCHAR2(32) NOT NULL,
                      FEATURE_ORDER NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      FEATURE_JSON CLOB CHECK (FEATURE_JSON IS JSON),
                      CONSTRAINT AGENT_MAP_RESULTS_PK
                          PRIMARY KEY (RUN_ID, FEATURE_ORDER)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'TREE_KMEANS_INPUT_V'
            AND object_type = 'VIEW' AND status = 'VALID';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW TREE_KMEANS_INPUT_V AS
                  SELECT SOURCE_RECORD_ID, TREE_AGE, TRUNK_DIAMETER
                  FROM BOMEN_TREES
                  WHERE SRT_WETENS = 'Quercus robur'
                    AND SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                    AND TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                    AND TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS_V'
            AND object_type = 'VIEW' AND status = 'VALID';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS_V AS
                  SELECT RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID, SPECIES_NAME, TREE_AGE,
                         TRUNK_DIAMETER, CLUSTER_ID, CLUSTER_PROBABILITY,
                         WGS84_LONGITUDE, WGS84_LATITUDE, CREATED_AT
                  FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS~';
          END IF;
      END prepare_tree_kmeans_storage;
      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## 2. Agent-callable build and score function


      Null species selects the Quercus robur pilot. Null cluster count selects

      three groups. A repeated request reuses a complete run with the same

      source signature and parameters. Force refresh is available for uncertain

      source changes. Each model rebuild replaces only
      TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL;

      saved RUN_ID rows remain available.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION tree_kmeans_agent_fn (
          p_species IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
          p_clusters IN NUMBER DEFAULT NULL,
          p_force_refresh IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'N'
      ) RETURN CLOB AS
          PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;
          v_species VARCHAR2(254) := NVL(TRIM(p_species), 'Quercus robur');
          v_clusters NUMBER := NVL(p_clusters, 3);
          v_force VARCHAR2(1) := UPPER(NVL(TRIM(p_force_refresh), 'N'));
          v_data_object_id NUMBER;
          v_source_count NUMBER;
          v_source_scn NUMBER;
          v_usable_count NUMBER;
          v_final_count NUMBER;
          v_final_scn NUMBER;
          v_model_count NUMBER;
          v_saved_count NUMBER;
          v_scored_count NUMBER;
          v_mappable_count NUMBER;
          v_map_count NUMBER;
          v_actual_clusters NUMBER;
          v_run_id VARCHAR2(32);
          v_reused VARCHAR2(1) := 'N';
          v_cluster_summary CLOB;
          v_response CLOB;
      BEGIN
          IF UPPER(v_species) <> 'QUERCUS ROBUR' THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20301,
                  'This K-means pilot supports Quercus robur only.');
          END IF;
          v_species := 'Quercus robur';
          IF v_clusters <> TRUNC(v_clusters)
             OR v_clusters < 2 OR v_clusters > 8 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20302,
                  'Clusters must be a whole number between 2 and 8.');
          END IF;
          IF v_force NOT IN ('Y', 'N') THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20303,
                  'p_force_refresh must be Y or N.');
          END IF;

          prepare_tree_kmeans_storage;
          SELECT data_object_id INTO v_data_object_id
          FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'BOMEN_TREES' AND object_type = 'TABLE';
          SELECT COUNT(*), NVL(MAX(ORA_ROWSCN), 0),
                 COUNT(CASE WHEN SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                             AND TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                             AND TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL THEN 1 END)
          INTO v_source_count, v_source_scn, v_usable_count
          FROM BOMEN_TREES WHERE SRT_WETENS = v_species;
          IF v_usable_count < 100 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20304,
                  'Fewer than 100 complete trees for the pilot species.');
          END IF;

          IF v_force = 'N' THEN
              BEGIN
                  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                      SELECT RUN_ID, SCORED_COUNT
                      FROM TREE_KMEANS_RUNS
                      WHERE SPECIES_NAME = :species
                        AND REQUESTED_CLUSTERS = :clusters
                        AND SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID = :object_id
                        AND SOURCE_ROW_COUNT = :row_count
                        AND SOURCE_MAX_SCN = :source_scn
                      ORDER BY CREATED_AT DESC
                      FETCH FIRST 1 ROW ONLY~'
                  INTO v_run_id, v_scored_count
                  USING v_species, v_clusters, v_data_object_id,
                        v_source_count, v_source_scn;
                  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                      SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS
                      WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
                  INTO v_saved_count USING v_run_id;
                  IF v_saved_count = v_scored_count
                     AND v_scored_count = v_usable_count THEN
                      v_reused := 'Y';
                  END IF;
              EXCEPTION WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN NULL;
              END;
          END IF;

          IF v_reused = 'N' THEN
              SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_model_count FROM user_mining_models
              WHERE model_name = 'TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL';
              IF v_model_count > 0 THEN
                  DBMS_DATA_MINING.DROP_MODEL('TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL');
              END IF;
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DELETE FROM TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS';
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'INSERT INTO TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS VALUES (:1, :2)'
                  USING DBMS_DATA_MINING.ALGO_NAME,
                        DBMS_DATA_MINING.ALGO_KMEANS;
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'INSERT INTO TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS VALUES (:1, :2)'
                  USING DBMS_DATA_MINING.CLUS_NUM_CLUSTERS,
                        TO_CHAR(v_clusters);
              COMMIT;

              DBMS_DATA_MINING.CREATE_MODEL(
                  model_name => 'TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL',
                  mining_function => DBMS_DATA_MINING.CLUSTERING,
                  data_table_name => 'TREE_KMEANS_INPUT_V',
                  case_id_column_name => 'SOURCE_RECORD_ID',
                  settings_table_name => 'TREE_KMEANS_SETTINGS'
              );

              v_run_id := RAWTOHEX(SYS_GUID());
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID, SPECIES_NAME, TREE_AGE,
                      TRUNK_DIAMETER, CLUSTER_ID, CLUSTER_PROBABILITY,
                      WGS84_LONGITUDE, WGS84_LATITUDE, GEOMETRY
                  )
                  SELECT :run_id, b.SOURCE_RECORD_ID, b.SRT_WETENS,
                         b.TREE_AGE, b.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                         CLUSTER_ID(TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL USING
                             b.TREE_AGE AS TREE_AGE,
                             b.TRUNK_DIAMETER AS TRUNK_DIAMETER),
                         CLUSTER_PROBABILITY(TREE_QUERCUS_KMEANS_MODEL USING
                             b.TREE_AGE AS TREE_AGE,
                             b.TRUNK_DIAMETER AS TRUNK_DIAMETER),
                         b.WGS84_LONGITUDE, b.WGS84_LATITUDE, b.GEOMETRY
                  FROM BOMEN_TREES b
                  WHERE b.SRT_WETENS = 'Quercus robur'
                    AND b.SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                    AND b.TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                    AND b.TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL~'
              USING v_run_id;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS
                  WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
              INTO v_scored_count USING v_run_id;
              SELECT COUNT(*), NVL(MAX(ORA_ROWSCN), 0)
              INTO v_final_count, v_final_scn
              FROM BOMEN_TREES WHERE SRT_WETENS = v_species;
              IF v_final_count <> v_source_count
                 OR v_final_scn <> v_source_scn THEN
                  RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20305,
                      'BOMEN_TREES changed during scoring; retry.');
              END IF;
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO TREE_KMEANS_RUNS (
                      RUN_ID, SPECIES_NAME, REQUESTED_CLUSTERS,
                      SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID, SOURCE_ROW_COUNT,
                      SOURCE_MAX_SCN, SCORED_COUNT
                  ) VALUES (:1, :2, :3, :4, :5, :6, :7)~'
              USING v_run_id, v_species, v_clusters, v_data_object_id,
                    v_source_count, v_source_scn, v_scored_count;
              COMMIT;
          END IF;

          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS
              WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id
                AND WGS84_LONGITUDE IS NOT NULL
                AND WGS84_LATITUDE IS NOT NULL~'
          INTO v_mappable_count USING v_run_id;
          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT COUNT(*) FROM AGENT_MAP_RESULTS
              WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
          INTO v_map_count USING v_run_id;
          IF v_map_count <> v_mappable_count THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  DELETE FROM AGENT_MAP_RESULTS
                  WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~' USING v_run_id;
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO AGENT_MAP_RESULTS
                      (RUN_ID, FEATURE_ORDER, FEATURE_JSON)
                  SELECT r.RUN_ID,
                         ROW_NUMBER() OVER
                             (ORDER BY r.CLUSTER_ID, r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID),
                         JSON_OBJECT(
                             'RUN_ID' VALUE r.RUN_ID,
                             'SOURCE_RECORD_ID' VALUE r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID,
                             'SPECIES_NAME' VALUE r.SPECIES_NAME,
                             'TREE_AGE' VALUE r.TREE_AGE,
                             'TRUNK_DIAMETER' VALUE r.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                             'CLUSTER_ID' VALUE r.CLUSTER_ID,
                             'CLUSTER_PROBABILITY' VALUE r.CLUSTER_PROBABILITY,
                             'GEOJSON' VALUE SDO_UTIL.TO_GEOJSON(
                                 MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY(
                                     2001, 4326,
                                     MDSYS.SDO_POINT_TYPE(
                                         r.WGS84_LONGITUDE,
                                         r.WGS84_LATITUDE, NULL
                                     ), NULL, NULL
                                 )
                             ) RETURNING CLOB
                         )
                  FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS r
                  WHERE r.RUN_ID = :run_id
                    AND r.WGS84_LONGITUDE IS NOT NULL
                    AND r.WGS84_LATITUDE IS NOT NULL~'
              USING v_run_id;
              COMMIT;
          END IF;

          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT CLUSTER_ID)
              FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
          INTO v_actual_clusters USING v_run_id;
          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT JSON_ARRAYAGG(
                         JSON_OBJECT(
                             'cluster_id' VALUE CLUSTER_ID,
                             'tree_count' VALUE N,
                             'min_tree_age' VALUE MIN_AGE,
                             'mean_tree_age' VALUE MEAN_AGE,
                             'max_tree_age' VALUE MAX_AGE,
                             'most_common_diameter_class' VALUE MODE_DIAMETER
                             RETURNING CLOB
                         ) ORDER BY CLUSTER_ID RETURNING CLOB)
              FROM (
                  SELECT CLUSTER_ID, COUNT(*) N,
                         MIN(TREE_AGE) MIN_AGE,
                         ROUND(AVG(TREE_AGE), 2) MEAN_AGE,
                         MAX(TREE_AGE) MAX_AGE,
                         STATS_MODE(TRUNK_DIAMETER) MODE_DIAMETER
                  FROM TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS
                  WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id
                  GROUP BY CLUSTER_ID
              )~'
          INTO v_cluster_summary USING v_run_id;
          SELECT JSON_OBJECT(
              'status' VALUE 'success',
              'run_id' VALUE v_run_id,
              'species' VALUE v_species,
              'requested_clusters' VALUE v_clusters,
              'actual_clusters' VALUE v_actual_clusters,
              'scored_trees' VALUE v_scored_count,
              'mapped_trees' VALUE v_mappable_count,
              'cache_reused' VALUE v_reused,
              'cluster_profiles' VALUE v_cluster_summary FORMAT JSON,
              'interpretation' VALUE
                  'Groups are based on recorded age and diameter class; they do not diagnose health or imply geographic continuity.'
              RETURNING CLOB
          ) INTO v_response FROM dual;
          RETURN v_response;
      END tree_kmeans_agent_fn;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 3. Tool, task, and worker

      No separate team is created. The task calls the tool once and uses the
      saved map rows from its returned RUN_ID. The test notebook contains the
      direct RUN_TOOL and team checks.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TOOL('TREE_KMEANS_TOOL', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TOOL(
              tool_name => 'TREE_KMEANS_TOOL',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "function":"TREE_KMEANS_AGENT_FN",
                  "instruction":"Group Quercus robur tree records by recorded age and trunk-diameter class. Save the scores and map points; return measured counts and RUN_ID. Groups are not health diagnoses.",
                  "tool_inputs":[
                      {"name":"p_species","description":"Optional species. This pilot accepts Quercus robur only; null uses Quercus robur."},
                      {"name":"p_clusters","description":"Optional whole number from 2 to 8. Null uses 3."},
                      {"name":"p_force_refresh","description":"Y rebuilds even when the source signature matches; otherwise N."}
                  ]
              }~',
              description => 'Saves and reuses Quercus robur K-means tree clusters.'
          );
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TASK: TREE_KMEANS_TASK

      DECLARE
          v_instruction VARCHAR2(4000) := q'|
      Answer the user's tree-grouping question: {query}

      1. This pilot supports Quercus robur in BOMEN_TREES only.

      2. Call TREE_KMEANS_TOOL exactly once for a supported request.

      3. Use the requested cluster count, or null for three groups.

      4. Rebuild only when requested; otherwise pass N.

      5. Report measured group sizes, scored/mapped counts, and RUN_ID.

      6. Do not describe clusters as unhealthy trees, anomaly flags, or
         necessarily neighbouring locations.
      7. The tool saves GeoJSON points for the map. Do not claim that the
         browser rendered them unless the application confirms it.
      |';
          v_attributes CLOB;
      BEGIN
          SELECT JSON_OBJECT(
              'instruction' VALUE v_instruction,
              'tools' VALUE JSON_ARRAY('TREE_KMEANS_TOOL') FORMAT JSON
              RETURNING CLOB
          ) INTO v_attributes FROM dual;
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TASK('TREE_KMEANS_TASK', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TASK(
              task_name => 'TREE_KMEANS_TASK',
              attributes => v_attributes,
              description => 'Groups Quercus robur trees by recorded age and diameter class.'
          );
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT('TREE_KMEANS_AGENT', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_KMEANS_AGENT',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name":"OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role":"You are the tree K-means worker. Follow TREE_KMEANS_TASK. Report measured cluster sizes and RUN_ID, and avoid health claims."
              }~',
              description => 'Tree K-means clustering worker.'
          );
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 4. Extend the existing supervised team

      Run after all four worker agents and their tasks exist. This is the only
      team rebuild in these new notebooks. It does not drop saved results or
      create another Ask Oracle team.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TEAM('TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT(
              'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR', force => TRUE
          );
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name":"OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role":"You supervise one Den Haag tree team. Route a request to the relevant worker: TREE_DISCOVERY_AGENT for an open-ended inspection of approved datasets; TREE_DENSITY_AGENT for neighbourhood tree density or green-area questions; TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT for Quercus robur one-class SVM review; TREE_KMEANS_AGENT for Quercus robur grouping by recorded age and trunk-diameter class. Ask a focused clarification when the requested analysis is unclear. For greetings, give brief examples of these four supported requests. Use measured tool results only. A discovery candidate or model group is not a health diagnosis. Do not claim the browser map rendered unless the application confirms it. Use only the relevant worker for a single-topic request.",
                  "supervisor":true
              }~',
              description => 'Routes discovery, density, anomaly, and K-means requests.'
          );
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TEAM(
              team_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "process":"sequential",
                  "supervisor_agent":"TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR",
                  "agents":[
                      {"name":"TREE_DISCOVERY_AGENT","task":"TREE_DISCOVERY_TASK"},
                      {"name":"TREE_DENSITY_AGENT","task":"TREE_DENSITY_TASK"},
                      {"name":"TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT","task":"TREE_ANOMALY_TASK"},
                      {"name":"TREE_KMEANS_AGENT","task":"TREE_KMEANS_TASK"}
                  ]
              }~',
              description => 'One supervised tree team with four specialist workers.'
          );
      END;

      /

      -- PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:01.380
    languageId: oracle-sql
